entry.summary:
Here's a bug I've shipped more than once: tests pass locally, demo looks great, seed data with foreign keys that don't actually
The quiet problem with hand-rolled seed data
Say you've got the classic Prisma setup: model User { id Int @id @default(autoincrement()) email String @unique posts Post[] }
model Post { id String @id @default(uuid()) title String author User @relation(fields: [authorId], references: [id]) authorId Int }
When you fake seed data for Post, what goes in authorId? If you're using a looks fine in a A JOIN between Post and User returns rows that shouldn't exist, or none at all. A real FK constraint in Postgres rejects the insert outright (violates foreign key constraint). Any UI that renders "post by author" either crashes or shows ghosts. Your seed data passed the eyeball test and failed the only test that matters: faker (and the dozens of wrappers around it) are great at generating values — relationships. They'll authorId: 8471 on a post when no user 8471 exists, because they To generate honest relational data you need to: Generate the parent rows first (User), and remember their real ids. Generate the child rows (Post), and set each authorId to an id that was actually generated for a user. It's not hard conceptually — it's just annoying to do by hand every single time I got tired of writing this glue, so I built a small VS Code extension, SeedForge, schema.prisma and generates the data for you. The free It's also on Open VSX if you're Even if you never touch SeedForge: next time you write seed data, ask whether JOINs will finally tell What's your approach to relational test data — hand-written factories, SQL fixtures, something else? Genuinely curious what's working for people.

Tired of export-ing env vars in every new terminal? Put your relay config in ~/.claude/settings.json under env, and Claude Code picks it up on launch:
{
  "env": {
    "ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL": "https://<station>",
    "ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN": "sk-****your-key****"
  }
}

Tips:
This file is local — don't commit it.
To juggle several stations, use ccswitch to keep each one on its own git branch and ccswitch switch between them.
If the model list won't load, add ANTHROPIC_MODEL with the exact id copied from the station.
Relay stations are free (signup + daily check-in credit) and plentiful — register a few. List with models and tested dates: AI relay station list
Signup links carry my referral param; strip ?aff= if you prefer.
